6. Renforcer les capacités des structures de santé pour assurer la supervision et la coordination des interventions de nutrition

Delivering WASH services targeting 10,000 IDPs in Salamiyah 1 Camp from """"Fondation Suez
"""" Comprehensive WASH response for conflict-affected vulnerable populations in Ninewa and Salah al Din Through this intervention, ACTED will contribute to the WASH Cluster’s objectives 1, 2, and 3:
1.	Restore, improve standards, and sustain water and sanitation services and provide an enabling environment for good hygiene practices to vulnerable individuals in protracted displacement and return settings;
2.	Provide safe and accessible emergency water and sanitation services and support good hygiene practices for highly vulnerable populations in and out of camps, new displacement and at risk areas after shocks;
3.	Facilitate the establishment of sustainable, cost effective, and equitable water and sanitation services including community-focused hygiene promotion, and facilitate take over of care and maintenance to communities and local authorities;

The project it is planned to complement ACTED’s multi-sectoral interventions in areas with a high prevalence of new returnees, vulnerable non-displaced families and households in protracted displacement. ACTED’s strategy for 2018 is based on the application of an area-based approach that allows to simultaneously address the different needs of vulnerable population groups in conflict-affected areas. 
For example, ACTED’s programming aims at re-establishing public service provision through Quick Impact Projects and the rehabilitation of communal WASH infrastructures; favouring returns through emergency repairs on private housing and distribution of core NFIs lost or damaged during displacement and looting; supporting IDPs willing to return and newly displaced households with multi-purpose cash assistance; creating income-generating opportunities through livelihoods interventions; and addressing urgent gaps in child protection through community-based approaches. 
Additionally, ACTED will provide in-camp and off-camp CCCM support, including the establishment of Urban Displacement Resource Centres in priority urban return areas.

Aide alimentaire d’urgence aux populations vulnérables de Ségou et Mopti. Appui à la restauration immédiate et au renforcement des moyens d’existence des ménages agricoles vulnérables affectés la crise sociopolitique et les changements climatiques au Nord et au Centre du Mali. L’objectif global est de restaurer et renforcer les capacités productives des ménages victimes, dont les femmes vulnérables chefs de ménage, du conflit et des inondations en phase de retour sur leurs exploitations agricoles et leur permettre ainsi de vivre dignement de l’agriculture pour la couverture de leurs besoins.
Objectif spécifique 1 : Appuyer la reprise de la production agricoles de base pour assurer la disponibilité alimentaire au niveau des ménages vulnérables par un apport d’intrants agricoles de base ;
Objectif spécifique 2 : Apporter l’assistance technique pour la diversification et l’amélioration de l’alimentation et des revenus par la promotion du maraîchage et de l’élevage à cycle court en faveur principalement des ménages dirigés par des femmes ;
Objectif spécifiques 3 : Réhabiliter les petits périmètres maraîchers (PPM) et périmètres irrigués villageois (PIV) pour accroître les capacités de production et de diversification des ressources alimentaires et monétaires.

